  /// to True, Managed Service for Apache Flink increases the
  /// CurrentParallelism value in response to application load. The service
  /// can increase the CurrentParallelism value up to the maximum parallelism,
  /// which is ParalellismPerKPU times the maximum KPUs for the application.
  /// The maximum KPUs for an application is 64 by default, and can be
  /// increased by requesting a limit increase. If application load is
  /// reduced, the service can reduce the CurrentParallelism value down to the
  /// Parallelism setting.
